94	/// See if we should dist this package.
95	///
96	/// Some(disabled_reason) is returned if it shouldn't be.
97	///
98	/// This code is written to assume a package and its binaries should be distable,
99	/// and then runs through a battery of disqualifying reasons.
100	///
101	/// A notable consequence of this is that if --tag wasn't passed, then we will default to
102	/// letting through all the packages that aren't intrinsically disqualified by things like
103	/// publish=false. Later steps will then check if a coherent announcement tag exists that
104	/// covers everything this function spat out.
105	fn check_dist_package(
106	    graph: &DistGraphBuilder,
107	    pkg_id: PackageIdx,
